 Applicability must depend on the Actor-visible question, actual source text, available local-tool observations or its own response, never a gold answer, grade or hidden optimizer state. Do not prescribe online lookup, code execution, new tools or scorer-assisted correction. A question or stated rationale can motivate a strategy but cannot establish unseen document contents or prove that preferring a table, date, field or longer answer is generally correct. Describe an unobserved document condition as a condition for the Actor to assess. Make a proposed procedure conditional and justify its burden within the real tool limits and 24-round budget.
 
-Preserve requested field roles, entity, relation, temporal basis, units, arithmetic operation and answer-granularity requirements. Do not replace the requested answer with an explanation, a list of guesses or a weaker deliverable. Answer completeness does not mean maximum length. Keep answer-element restrictions scoped to that element and preserve the no-further-tool final-answer protocol; no extra explanation is required. Differences in units, punctuation, date or numeric representation may explain a string mismatch only where observable evidence supports it and the native scorer distinguishes it; they do not justify universal normalization rules.
+Keep answer-element restrictions scoped to that element and preserve the no-further-tool final-answer protocol; no extra explanation is required.
 
 Goal states the intended improvement and necessary preservation boundaries without making an untested strategy immutable. Every Update carries its material trigger, action, strength, exceptions, dependencies and preservation conditions. Distinguish permission, preference and obligation. Do not encode task IDs, instance answers or question-to-answer lookup keys, nor turn an isolated observed spelling into a universal rule.
 
